WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:28.760
LLM's map land versus water from pure text latitude, longitude pairs with no images at all. This is Models &amp; Agents, episode 191. Andre Carpathy showed that large language models can correctly classify land versus water, when given only latitude and longitude as text. The evaluation queried models 16,200 times across a grid, and rendered the answers as an image that closely matches real geography.

00:00:28.760 --> 00:00:34.020
The result demonstrates that factual spatial knowledge emerges from compressing internet

00:00:34.020 --> 00:00:34.860
text alone.

00:00:35.480 --> 00:00:39.060
No vision training or image data was involved in the models tested.

00:00:39.820 --> 00:00:45.080
Builders can reproduce the test with any frontier model by feeding coordinate strings and

00:00:45.080 --> 00:00:45.920
plotting outputs.

00:00:46.640 --> 00:00:52.380
The finding reinforces that scale on text continues to unlock structured world knowledge without

00:00:52.380 --> 00:00:53.620
multimodal input.

00:00:53.620 --> 00:01:01.020
In model updates, CarPathy ran the same land or water query across multiple models, including all

00:01:01.020 --> 00:01:06.800
clawed variants. Results were aggregated into a single image that reveals accurate coastline

00:01:06.800 --> 00:01:14.340
and continent boundaries. The experiment used 16,200 coordinate pairs and required no images or

00:01:14.340 --> 00:01:20.900
maps during training or inference. GraphForge builds tasks from real files and an evidence graph,

00:01:20.900 --> 00:01:26.020
graph, so both the task and its verification rubrics are grounded in the same documents.

00:01:26.660 --> 00:01:38.740
Fine-tuning Quinn 3.627b on 2,169 trajectories raised GDP-val to 1,445.7 under open hands.

00:01:39.280 --> 00:01:43.700
It also improved workspace bench light and spreadsheet bench two scores.

00:01:44.400 --> 00:01:46.600
The data and models are released publicly.

00:01:46.600 --> 00:01:52.560
Settle trains the end of reasoning token on answer stability observed in completed traces.

00:01:53.080 --> 00:02:00.380
On Math 500 with Quinn 34b, it cut token count by 40% while accuracy dropped only half

00:02:00.380 --> 00:02:01.320
a percentage point.

00:02:01.980 --> 00:02:05.540
The method requires only ordinary decoding at inference time.

00:02:06.200 --> 00:02:12.180
The authors of the Co-T alignment paper introduce Co-T interpretability alignment as a metric

00:02:12.180 --> 00:02:17.660
comparing chain-of-thought traces to internal reasoning detected by imperperability tools.

00:02:18.260 --> 00:02:25.460
Baseline alignment across three casks and three models ranged from 44.8% to 75.9%.

00:02:26.120 --> 00:02:31.520
Post-training with both accuracy and faithfulness rewards improved parametric faithfulness

00:02:31.520 --> 00:02:38.180
while preserving task performance. French requires 31% to 58% more tokens than English

00:02:38.180 --> 00:02:46.360
across 72026 tokenizers. Regional languages of France pay roughly 1.6 to 3.3 times the English

00:02:46.360 --> 00:02:54.840
token count. A bite-level BPE prototype called Baracoda FR version 1.2 reduces the French premium by

00:02:54.840 --> 00:03:04.040
11.5% relative to Tekken, while using 3.7% fewer tokens on English. Seed choice moved fairness metrics

00:03:04.040 --> 00:03:11.500
more than audio compression on most demographic axes, when fine-tuning speech LLMs on 460 hours

00:03:11.500 --> 00:03:19.000
of Libre speech. 85.3% of the variation in fair speech ethnicity-normalized gap was attributed

00:03:19.000 --> 00:03:25.900
to seed rather than compression. Scaling the adaptation set to 960 hours reduced but did not

00:03:25.900 --> 00:03:32.220
eliminate the effect. In agent and tool developments, Autosynth data turns a target model's failures

00:03:32.220 --> 00:03:39.720
and a stronger teacher successes into new training tasks that exercise the same capability in varied situations.

00:03:40.540 --> 00:03:47.240
Tasks are generated inside Enterprise Ops Gym and validated for feasibility against the environment specification.

00:03:48.000 --> 00:03:52.420
The curriculum shifts automatically toward remaining weaknesses as the model improves.

00:03:52.420 --> 00:04:01.740
RSI game runs local Explorer Diagnose improved loops alongside a global loop that preserves the best checkpoint and detects saturation.

00:04:02.500 --> 00:04:08.860
Across 140 gamecraft bench tasks, it raised quality on two engines and five generators.

00:04:09.440 --> 00:04:20.400
Experience internalization let Quinn 3.827B exceed GPT 5.5 one-shot scores while using 11 times fewer generation tokens.

00:04:20.400 --> 00:04:27.240
The EVCALC system reads PDFs, selects passages, asks a language model to write arithmetic

00:04:27.240 --> 00:04:29.880
expressions, and evaluates them locally.

00:04:30.600 --> 00:04:37.140
It achieved 8.61% joint accuracy on the official test set of 1,730 tasks.

00:04:37.760 --> 00:04:44.420
A public validation run reached 92.17% answer accuracy with perfect evidence F1.

00:04:44.420 --> 00:04:49.880
Criteria extraction was compared with chain of thought prompting on two-reddit corpora

00:04:49.880 --> 00:04:53.580
using PHQ9 and BDI2 questionnaires.

00:04:54.260 --> 00:04:59.640
For frontier models, the extraction approach showed no significant gain once decision thresholds

00:04:59.640 --> 00:05:02.800
were fixed, a priority from the questionnaire criteria.

00:05:03.460 --> 00:05:08.800
The 9 billion parameter model labeled most post-severe regardless of prompting style on

00:05:08.800 --> 00:05:09.480
one corpus.

00:05:09.480 --> 00:05:17.920
In practical and community, CarPathy recommends asking models to explain concepts in ASD-ST-E100

00:05:17.920 --> 00:05:23.740
controlled language for cleaner output. He suggests requesting HTML for interactive web

00:05:23.740 --> 00:05:31.560
pages and custom 3B1B style explainer videos that use 11 labs narration. The approach treats large,

00:05:31.800 --> 00:05:37.020
custom software artifacts as cheap and discardable once intelligence and code become abundant.

00:05:37.760 --> 00:05:44.180
Carpathy stressed that all observed capabilities arise from reading large amounts of text and predicting the next token.

00:05:44.940 --> 00:05:49.120
Image-like arrangements appear only in the two-dimensional layout of text responses.

00:05:49.820 --> 00:05:55.160
The point underscores that spatial and factual knowledge can emerge without any visual training data.

00:05:55.880 --> 00:06:00.060
Bitdefender released a beta of AI Guardian that runs on Mac agents.

00:06:00.700 --> 00:06:05.420
The tool focuses on detecting and containing rogue agent behavior at the endpoint level.

00:06:05.420 --> 00:06:11.380
DigiCert announced new certificate and identity controls intended to give organizations visibility

00:06:11.380 --> 00:06:16.360
and revocation options when autonomous agents act outside intended boundaries.

00:06:17.180 --> 00:06:20.860
Pop the hood on tokenization trade-offs in multilingual settings.

00:06:21.480 --> 00:06:27.100
Bite-paring coding builds a vocabulary by repeatedly merging the most frequent adjacent symbol pairs

00:06:27.100 --> 00:06:33.120
until a target size is reached. The resulting token boundaries reflect training data statistics

00:06:33.120 --> 00:06:38.480
rather than linguistic structure, so languages with different orthographies or morphologies

00:06:38.480 --> 00:06:44.620
pay different token counts for the same meaning. Adding French data to a tokenizer training run

00:06:44.620 --> 00:06:50.220
reduces the French premium within the first few thousand merges but increases the English token

00:06:50.220 --> 00:06:57.020
count as vocabulary slots are reallocated. The effect plateaus after roughly 50,000 merges

00:06:57.020 --> 00:07:01.580
while the English cost keeps rising, creating a direct capacity trade-off.

00:07:02.040 --> 00:07:07.060
At inference time, the higher token count directly raises both latency and cost,

00:07:07.480 --> 00:07:12.980
because billing and context windows are measured in tokens. When a workload is known to be French

00:07:12.980 --> 00:07:18.760
heavy, training a dedicated tokenizer or fine-tuning an existing one on French text yields the

00:07:18.760 --> 00:07:23.840
largest reduction. Otherwise, the marginal gain rarely justifies the English penalty.

00:07:23.840 --> 00:07:29.340
Team should measure the actual token ratio on their target corpus before committing to

00:07:29.340 --> 00:07:31.320
a multilingual tokenizer change.

00:07:31.680 --> 00:07:38.880
Try asking any frontier model to rewrite an explanation in ASD-ST-100 controlled language

00:07:39.190 --> 00:07:41.840
and compare readability with the default output.

00:07:42.850 --> 00:07:47.860
Reproduce Carpathi's land or water coordinate test on your preferred model and plot the

00:07:47.860 --> 00:07:51.120
results to see geographic knowledge emerge from text alone.

00:07:51.120 --> 00:07:57.080
Find Tune a small open-weight model on the released graph-forged trajectories to test

00:07:57.080 --> 00:07:59.740
agent performance on real-file workspaces.

00:08:00.540 --> 00:08:06.560
Generate a custom 3B1B style explainer video prompt for a topic you are teaching and test

00:08:06.560 --> 00:08:08.640
it with an 11-labs API key.

